# COLFIO Design Principles

This rule encodes the architectural principles extracted from the Tetris and Vlak reference implementations. All new game code must follow these principles.

Reference documentation: `docs/11-game-architecture.md`, `docs/12-tetris-case-study.md`, `docs/13-vlak-case-study.md`

---

## 1. Single Responsibility Per Component

Each component does exactly **one thing**. Split any component that handles more than one concern.

```typescript
// WRONG — one component doing three jobs
class GameComponent extends ECS.Component {
    onUpdate() {
        this.handleInput();  // input
        this.updatePhysics(); // physics
        this.drawScore();    // rendering
    }
}

// CORRECT — three separate components
class PlayerInputController extends ECS.Component { /* input only */ }
class PhysicsUpdater extends ECS.Component { /* physics only */ }
class ScoreRenderer extends ECS.Component { /* rendering only */ }
```

---

## 2. Model/State Separation from ECS

Model and state classes are **plain TypeScript** — they must never extend `ECS.Component` or hold a reference to any component.

```typescript
// WRONG — model coupled to ECS
class GameModel extends ECS.Component { ... }

// CORRECT — model is pure TypeScript
class GameModel {
    score = 0;
    lives = 3;
    level = 1;
}

// CORRECT — state may hold a scene reference to send messages (ObservableState pattern)
class GameState {
    constructor(private scene: ECS.Scene) {}
    addScore(pts: number) {
        this.score += pts;
        this.scene.sendMessage(new ECS.Message(Messages.SCORE_CHANGED, null, null, this.score));
    }
}
```

---

## 3. Message-Driven Communication Between Components

Components **never hold direct references to each other**. All inter-component communication goes through the message bus.

```typescript
// WRONG — direct coupling
class PlayerController extends ECS.Component {
    renderer: GameRenderer; // never do this
    onUpdate() { this.renderer.updateScore(100); }
}

// CORRECT — decoupled via messages
class PlayerController extends ECS.Component {
    onUpdate() {
        if (this.scored) {
            this.sendMessage(Messages.SCORE_CHANGED, newScore);
        }
    }
}
class GameRenderer extends ECS.Component {
    onInit() { this.subscribe(Messages.SCORE_CHANGED); }
    onMessage(msg: ECS.Message) { this.drawScore(msg.data); }
}
```

---

## 4. Factory for Scene Transitions

All scene setup and transitions go through the `Factory` class. Never build entities or clear the scene inline (e.g. inside a component update without deferral).

```typescript
// WRONG — scene creation scattered in a component
class SomeComponent extends ECS.Component {
    onMessage(msg) {
        scene.clearScene(); // ERROR: can't clear during update loop
        new ECS.Builder(scene).asSprite(...).build(); // entity created inline
    }
}

// CORRECT — deferred delegation to Factory
class SomeComponent extends ECS.Component {
    onMessage(msg) {
        if (msg.action === Messages.GAME_OVER) {
            this.scene.callWithDelay(0, () => new Factory().loadIntro(this.scene));
        }
    }
}
```

---

## 5. Builder Pattern for Entity Construction

All game object construction uses `ECS.Builder` fluent API. Never construct an entity and manually configure it with separate statements scattered outside a builder function.

```typescript
// WRONG — manual fragmented construction
const sprite = new ECS.Sprite('player', texture);
sprite.position.x = 100;
sprite.position.y = 200;
sprite.addComponent(new PlayerController(model));
sprite.addTag('player');
scene.stage.addChild(sprite);

// CORRECT — declarative builder in builders.ts
static playerBuilder = (scene: ECS.Scene, model: GameModel) =>
    new ECS.Builder(scene)
        .withName('player')
        .asSprite(PIXI.Texture.from(Assets.SPRITESHEET))
        .anchor(0.5)
        .localPos(model.spawnX, model.spawnY)
        .withTag(Tags.PLAYER)
        .withComponent(new PlayerController(model))
        .withParent(scene.stage);
```

---

## 6. Selectors for Global State Access

Always use a `Selectors` class to access global attributes. Never call `getGlobalAttribute` with raw string literals scattered across multiple files.

```typescript
// WRONG — raw string repeated everywhere
const state = this.scene.getGlobalAttribute<GameState>('GAME_STATE');
const keys  = this.scene.getGlobalAttribute<ECS.KeyInputComponent>('key_input');

// CORRECT — centralized typed access
// selectors.ts
export class Selectors {
    static gameState = (scene: ECS.Scene) =>
        scene.getGlobalAttribute<GameState>(Attributes.GAME_STATE);
    static keyInput = (scene: ECS.Scene) =>
        scene.getGlobalAttribute<ECS.KeyInputComponent>(Attributes.KEY_INPUT);
}

// Usage anywhere
const state = Selectors.gameState(this.scene);
```

---

## 7. Actions for Multi-Step Sequences

Any async or multi-step game flow (waiting, transitioning, animating then acting) must return a `ChainComponent` from an `Actions` class. Never use `setTimeout` or `setInterval`.

```typescript
// WRONG
setTimeout(() => this.doSomething(), 2000);
setInterval(() => this.doRepeat(), 500);

// WRONG — inline chains scattered in components
this.scene.addGlobalComponentAndRun(new ECS.ChainComponent()
    .waitTime(2000)
    .call(() => new Factory().loadGame(this.scene)));

// CORRECT — defined in actions.ts
export class Actions {
    static gameOver = (scene: ECS.Scene) =>
        new ECS.ChainComponent()
            .call((cmp) => cmp.sendMessage(Messages.GAME_OVER))
            .waitTime(2000)
            .waitFor(() => new FadeOutAnimation())
            .call(() => scene.callWithDelay(0, () => new Factory().loadIntro(scene)));
}

// Usage in a component
this.scene.addGlobalComponentAndRun(Actions.gameOver(this.scene));
```

---

## 8. Enums for All String Keys

Messages, tags, attributes, and asset keys must be `enum` values. Never use raw string literals.

```typescript
// WRONG
this.subscribe('game_over');
this.sendMessage('score_changed', newScore);
scene.assignGlobalAttribute('gameState', state);
scene.findObjectsByTag('player');

// CORRECT
export enum Messages { GAME_OVER = 'GAME_OVER', SCORE_CHANGED = 'SCORE_CHANGED' }
export enum Tags { PLAYER = 'player', ENEMY = 'enemy' }
export enum Attributes { GAME_STATE = 'GAME_STATE', KEY_INPUT = 'KEY_INPUT' }

this.subscribe(Messages.GAME_OVER);
this.sendMessage(Messages.SCORE_CHANGED, newScore);
scene.assignGlobalAttribute(Attributes.GAME_STATE, state);
scene.findObjectsByTag(Tags.PLAYER);
```

---

## 9. Typed Component Props

Always type the generic parameter of `Component<T>`. Never use `Component<any>` or `Component<void>` when the component needs to operate on a model.

```typescript
// WRONG — untyped, fragile
class EnemyAI extends ECS.Component<any> {
    onUpdate() { (this.props as any).health--; }
}

// CORRECT — fully typed
class EnemyAI extends ECS.Component<EnemyState> {
    onUpdate() { this.props.takeDamage(10); }
}
```

---

## 10. No PIXI Manipulation Outside Renderer Components

Direct PIXI property changes (`position`, `texture`, `alpha`, `visible`, `tint`) belong only inside **renderer** or **sync** components. Controllers and model classes must not touch PIXI display properties.

```typescript
// WRONG — controller modifying display
class PlayerController extends ECS.Component<PlayerState> {
    onUpdate() {
        this.props.move();
        this.owner.position.x = this.props.x; // display manipulation in controller
        this.owner.alpha = this.props.isDead ? 0 : 1;
    }
}

// CORRECT — separated sync component
class PlayerController extends ECS.Component<PlayerState> {
    onUpdate() { this.props.move(); } // only mutates state
}
class PlayerSyncComponent extends ECS.Component<PlayerState> {
    onUpdate() {
        this.owner.position.x = this.props.x; // display sync only
        this.owner.alpha = this.props.isDead ? 0 : 1;
    }
}
```

---

## 11. `finish()` for Self-Termination

Never call `removeComponent` on yourself. Use `this.finish()` to self-terminate a component.

```typescript
// WRONG
this.owner.removeComponent(this);

// CORRECT
this.finish();
```

---

## 12. `callWithDelay` for Safe Deferred Execution

Never use `setTimeout`. Never call `clearScene()` directly inside an update loop.

```typescript
// WRONG
setTimeout(() => this.scene.clearScene(), 1000);

// WRONG — throws Error during update loop
this.scene.clearScene();

// CORRECT
this.scene.callWithDelay(1000, () => {
    this.scene.clearScene();
    new Factory().loadGame(this.scene);
});

// CORRECT — ChainComponent deferred approach
scene.addGlobalComponentAndRun(new ECS.ChainComponent()
    .waitTime(1000)
    .call(() => scene.callWithDelay(0, () => new Factory().loadGame(scene)))
);
```

---

## Folder Responsibilities Summary

| File | Must contain | Must NOT contain |
|------|-------------|-----------------|
| `index.ts` | Engine config, asset loading | Game logic, entity creation |
| `constants.ts` | Enums (Messages, Tags, Assets, Attributes, Flags) | Logic, imports from ECS |
| `factory.ts` | `clearScene()`, global component setup, delegation to Builders | PIXI creation code, business logic |
| `builders.ts` | `ECS.Builder` factory functions | `clearScene()`, state logic |
| `selectors.ts` | `getGlobalAttribute` wrappers | Mutations, logic |
| `actions.ts` | `ChainComponent` factory functions | Direct PIXI manipulation |
| `helpers.ts` | Pure utility functions | ECS imports, state mutations |
| `model/game-structs.ts` | `type`, `interface`, `enum` definitions | Classes with methods, ECS imports |
| `model/game-state.ts` | Mutable state with `sendMessage` | Component extends, rendering |
| `components/*.ts` | Single-responsibility behavior | Multiple concerns, direct component refs |
